From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unom <packages@unom.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:13:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 46/46] punktfunk: stamp pfhdr39

A banner shows whether a box lays a planar capture's chroma on a row the
Intel encoder reads. An older gamescope streams 1080 rows with the colour
16 rows too high there. No new capability.
---
 src/meson.build | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index ffcfa51..395c548 100644
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -231,7 +231,8 @@ vcs_tag = run_command(vcs_tag_cmd, check: false).stdout().strip()
 #   +pfhdr36 — …and the WSI layer reports an X11 window's size as its extent range
 #   +pfhdr37 — …and a refresh with a fraction (-r 59.94) runs to the millihertz
 #   +pfhdr38 — …and Intel is told a LINEAR capture image is exported (Xe2 compressed it)
-version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr38' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
+#   +pfhdr39 — …and a planar capture's chroma starts on a 16-row boundary on Intel
+version_tag = vcs_tag + '+pfhdr39' + ' (' + compiler_name + ' ' + compiler_version + ')'
 
 gamescope_version_conf = configuration_data()
 gamescope_version_conf.set('VCS_TAG', version_tag)
